# SITL run artifacts. These are regenerated on every run, and eeprom.bin in
# particular conflicts constantly - it is a binary that the simulator rewrites
# whenever anything is changed in flight.
#
# Nothing here needs to be kept: PhoenixSITL.parm holds the tuning, and the
# mission and fence are loaded from orroral4.txt / southnamadgi.txt and
# instrument_fence.txt. To rebuild the vehicle state from scratch:
#
#     rm eeprom.bin && ./go-headless.sh
#     wp load orroral4.txt
#     fence load instrument_fence.txt
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so the deliberate snapshots under Archive/
# stay tracked.
/eeprom*.bin

# per-run logs and MAVProxy output
/logs/
PhoenixSITL/logs/
/PhoenixSITL-headless/
/mav.parm
/mav_*.parm
/mav.tlog
/mav.tlog.raw
